Why AGPL-3.0? This is the standard license for non-profit, public-interest
software (used by Wikipedia's MediaWiki, Nextcloud, Element, etc.). The
network copyleft clause ensures that any organisation running a modified
version of this site must publish their improvements back to the community,
which is consistent with WWF's non-profit mission. A weaker license (MIT,
Apache-2.0) would allow commercial entities to take this code, modify it,
and not contribute back.
